{"body":"\u003ca href=\"#\"\u003e\u003cimg alt=\"P1\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e **Slotted graphs select wrong items**\n\nIf `options.el` is slotted into a custom element, this walk jumps straight from the container to its host. It skips the slot and its shadow-tree parents, so a rotation or active motion path on a wrapper around the slot goes unchecked.\n\nThe canvas’s rotated bounding rectangle is then treated as axis-aligned. Clicking a visible node can select something else or clear selection instead of passing through without a command. Follow `assignedSlot` before `parentElement`, or reject slotted containers, and add a regression for a transformed wrapper around a slot.\n\n**Knowledge Base Used:** [GraphForge interaction sessions](https://app.greptile.com/-/switch-tenant?tenant=curatelabs\u0026next=%2Fcustom-context%2Fknowledge-base%2Fcuratelabs%2Fxyg%2F-%2Fdocs%2Fgraphforge-interaction-sessions.md)\n\n","commit_id":"da52bca32651077ddf53d9fdd014245731b6d087","created_at":"2026-11-04T02:57:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/CurateLabs/xyg/pull/1092#discussion_r4463052824","id":4463052824,"line":188,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOTxX6Es8AAAABCgTIGA","path":"js/src/63_graph_controller.ts","updated_at":"2026-11-04T02:57:02Z"}
